<title>USA: Abbott blood device gets market clearance.</title>
<headline>Abbott blood device gets market clearance.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH CHICAGO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abbott Laboratories Inc said Friday it received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market Cell-Dyne 4000, a device which monitors cell count in blood.</p>
<p>The device is expected to be available in the first quarter 1997, a company spokesman said. It will be marketed to laboratories and hospitals.</p>
<p>Shares of Abbott, a huge health care products company, closed off one to 50.</p>
<p>Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
